    "knowledge_point": "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix",
    "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
    "worked_solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{21}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -8 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -10 & -11 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-7{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-8{R}_{2}.$",
